// The perm-sign side condition of `acc(x.f, p)` is discharged from the facts
// established by *earlier* parts of the same specification: `0/1 < p` is stated
// before the `acc`, so `p` is provably non-negative by the time the obligation
// `not (p < 0/1)` is raised.
//
// The bridge from the strict fact to the non-strict obligation is the
// `lt-asymmetry-real` rule (`verify/rewrite/arith.rs`): the assumed class
// `0/1 <r p` pins its mirror `p <r 0/1` false, and `ite-reduce` collapses the
// negation. Before that rule this was a known limitation — the side condition saw
// the preceding conjunct but had no order theory to use it.
//
// Was tests/cases/known_limitations/, promoted 2026-08-20.

field f: Int

method n(x: Ref, p: Perm)
    requires 0/1 < p
    requires acc(x.f, p)
{}
